  "notes": "カット is a very common loanword from English \"cut,\" used both as a noun and as a suru verb (カットする).\n\nSENSE 1 — HAIRCUT:\nAt hair salons, カット refers specifically to the cutting service. Pricing menus typically list カット separately from other services.\n\nSENSE 2 — DELETION/REDUCTION:\nUsed in film editing, business cost-cutting, and general removal of content.\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- ヘアカット: haircut\n- コストカット: cost cutting\n- {賃金|ちんぎん}カット: wage cut\n- カット{野菜|やさい}: pre-cut vegetables",
